        "Validate and normalize input at the API boundary (server-side validation is required even if you validate on the client).",
        "Use a validation library (e.g., Joi or Celebrate) to enforce schemas and constraints.",
        "Protect against NoSQL injection: remove or reject keys that start with $ or contain dots in query/filter objects. Use middleware like express-mongo-sanitize.",
        "Use parameterized-like query patterns with Mongoose to avoid building queries by concatenating strings.",
        "Escape or sanitize any content that will be rendered back to clients when direct rendering might occur."
      ]
    },
    {
      "area": "Database - MongoDB",
      "points": [
        "Define strict Mongoose schemas with required fields, types, enums, and default values.",
        "Enable collection-level validation where possible (JSON Schema validation).",
        "Whitelist fields in queries and projections; never return sensitive/internal fields by default.",
        "Guard against NoSQL injection by sanitizing input (e.g., using express-mongo-sanitize) before it reaches query builders.",
        "Store sanitized or minimally necessary data; avoid echoing back large raw payloads."
      ]
    },
    {
      "area": "API Security & Networking",
      "points": [
        "Apply security headers with Helmet (Content-Security-Policy, X-Content-Type-Options, etc.).",
